# Local model profile — 2026-10-06, Apple M1 / 8 GB, Ollama 0.23.2.
# Loaded after .env; environment and .env take precedence. Restart after changes.
# These are saved-capture experiments, NOT a room-level accuracy certification.
VISION_PROVIDER=detector
DETECTOR_MODEL=yolo26s.pt
VALIDATOR_DETECTOR_MODEL=yolo11s.pt
ROOM_DETECTOR_MODEL=library-room-yoloe26s-v2.pt
BOOK_READER_MODEL=qwen2.5vl:3b
OLLAMA_URL=http://localhost:11434
OCR_ROLE_MODEL=
ENABLE_ROOM_DETAIL_READER=false

# SELECTED: YOLO26s primary localization + YOLO11s supplementary book boxes.
# Independent agreement uses ORIGINAL primary boxes, not the supplemented set.
# The models share COCO biases. Large covers can be mislabelled as phones.
# Suspect rectangles with OCR evidence receive a local crop-title check.
# SELECTED: YOLOE26s with fused room prompts for shelving, furniture, appliances,
# lighting, art, rugs, electronics and decor. Categories are unverified proposals;
# models can confuse TVs/mirrors and duplicate partially occluded objects.
# SELECTED: Apple Vision crop OCR, choosing one coherent reading orientation.
# SELECTED: Qwen2.5-VL 3B for cropped TITLE proposals; author/publisher constrained
# to exact OCR text choices. Do not use generated prices, editions or metric dimensions.
# Full 29-frame saved-evidence replay: 88.87 seconds; three distinct proposed titles
# persisted after the final empty view. This precedes the stricter OCR-choice
# author pass (20.1/21.6/12.0 s on three crops). Repeated crops reuse local results.
# This recording is not the required 60-book/eight-item benchmark.

# TESTED ALTERNATIVES, commented out with observed limitations:
# OCR_ROLE_MODEL=qwen2.5:3b
# Worked on isolated English/Hindi OCR-line tests (2.838 / 6.223 s), but rotating
# OCR mixtures caused invalid indices/abstentions. Co-residency with the 3B VLM
# caused timeouts on this 8 GB Mac. The text-only path remains optional in code.
# OCR_ROLE_MODEL=qwen2.5:1.5b
# Abstained on readable Hindi crop text and an English title in smoke tests.
# OCR_ROLE_MODEL=gemma3:1b
# Returned invalid/overlapping indices and omitted a book (6.230 s smoke test).
# DETECTOR_MODEL=yolo26m.pt
# Larger was worse on these captures: classified the black cover as a phone/
# laptop and gave the held Hindi book lower confidence. Warm detector 0.282 s.
# DETECTOR_MODEL=yolo11s.pt
# Not primary: overlapping book/keyboard/laptop labels; retained as a second
# source of book boxes, not a veto or proof of identity.
# ROOM_DETECTOR_MODEL=library-room-yoloe26s.pt
# Earlier prompts omitted structural negatives. V2 adds doors/windows/walls;
# both versions can still mistake TV/mirror categories and need review.
# ENABLE_ROOM_DETAIL_READER=true
# Numbered crop contact sheets timed out or shifted labels (cup became chair).
# Five-view trial reached 58 s/frame. Disabled; material/brand need human evidence.
# BOOK_READER_MODEL=qwen3-vl:2b
# Produced only thinking, no JSON answer, before a 160-token cap despite
# think=false. Do not claim its general accuracy is inferior; this path failed.
# VISION_PROVIDER=ollama
# OLLAMA_VISION_MODEL=qwen2.5vl:3b
# Whole-frame count/detail generation took 430.235 s in an earlier replay, with
# invented author text and item timeout. Cropped title reading is a different,
# bounded task; unrestricted author/publisher generation also failed crop probes.
# VALIDATOR_MODEL=moondream:latest
# Returned one book on a blank white negative control and disagreed on saved
# captures. Rejected as default count validator; legacy implementation retained.
# OLLAMA_VISION_MODEL=gemma3:latest
# Earlier 32.8 s probe grouped a three-book stack as one entry, with blank titles.
# OLLAMA_VISION_MODEL=moondream:latest
# Same failed blank-frame control as above; not selected for primary inventory.

# INSTALLED / CONSIDERED, no comparable completed benchmark:
# OLLAMA_VISION_MODEL=qwen3-vl:8b
# 6.1 GB weights leave too little room for context, OCR, browser, detectors and OS
# on this 8 GB Mac. No full-pipeline performance claim.
# OLLAMA_VISION_MODEL=qwen3.5:2b
# Could not test: Ollama rejected its manifest with HTTP 412 (newer runtime
# required). No system Ollama upgrade was performed.
# VISION_PROVIDER=photon
# MOONDREAM_MODEL=moondream3.1-9B-A2B
# No fit/performance validation on this machine; not loaded/tested.
# MLX-VLM: not installed; adding another runtime is an unvalidated dependency path.

# OCR language experiment: forcing English caused timeouts and damaged Hindi.
# Native automatic language detection remains selected. OCR can still be wrong.
# Official sources: https://docs.ultralytics.com/models/yolo26/
# https://docs.ultralytics.com/models/yoloe/
# https://ollama.com/library/qwen2.5vl:3b
# Ultralytics: AGPL-3.0 / Enterprise; review licenses before distribution.

# Context-aware spoken dialogue, separate from vision and evidence rules.
CONVERSATION_MODEL=qwen2.5:3b

# Six identical saved crops compared before enabling this separate verifier.
# Gemma 4B produced one accepted TV label with the parts-support gate, and no
# accepted incorrect names. It also guessed wrong categories: conflicts remain
# excluded. This targeted regression is not an accuracy certification.
# Qwen3-VL 8B timed out on all six crops (60s/request) on this 8GB Mac.
CROP_VERIFIER_MODEL=gemma3:latest
CROP_VERIFIER_TIMEOUT_S=45
CROP_VERIFICATION_FRAME_BUDGET_S=90
